{:name "app-base"
 :version "1.0.0"
 :description "App-server foundation: the reitit route-building vocabulary (generic `:route` / `:route-with-middleware`, the per-method templates, and the auth-required presets) plus small shared response helpers (`:assoc-status`, health). Split out of `app` so consumers that only need the route templates — the tenancy addon, the registry — do not have to depend on the whole editor package."
 ;; Only core (`:assoc` / `:list`) and web (`:auth-required-middleware`,
 ;; response matrix) — deliberately NO `app` dependency, so this is a
 ;; genuine lower layer `app` (and addons) build ON, not a relabel.
 ;; The fn `:namespace`s stay `app.common` / `app.routes.method` /
 ;; `app.routes.auth` unchanged: identity is `uuid-v5(namespace, name)`,
 ;; so moving only the package DIRECTORY leaves every id + every ref
 ;; resolution byte-identical — no remint, no `:post`/`:delete`
 ;; collision-resolution change.
 :dependencies ["core" "web"]
 :modules ["common" "routes-method" "routes-auth"]}
